The propulsion model in src/physics/buoyancy/forces.ts (vectored thrust with prop
ventilation, heel and advance-ratio losses, speed-dependent steering, rudder
lift and planing lift) and the boat values in src/presets/buoyancy.ts
(runabout from "zefiro", motor-yacht from "motoryacht") are adapted from
open-water (https://github.com/bob6664569/open-water, commit
285b6ce32057c70191a7fe16c31d979fa383ac64, site/js/simulation/boat.js and
vessels.js). Buoyancy, drag and damping are rewritten for 3D Clip Studio as
Archimedes probe columns applied to Rapier rigid bodies; the column method
follows the bounded probe model described for FusionWater-style floaters and
J. Kerner, "Water interaction model for boats in video games" (2015). No
open-water models (CC BY-NC) are included.

